Subject: [PATCH] XHCI: Enhanced features, quirks detection, and USB 3.1+ support

Implement comprehensive improvements to the xHCI driver based on Linux and
FreeBSD implementations for better hardware compatibility and reliability.

Changes:

1. Controller quirks detection system:
   - Detect vendor-specific quirks based on PCI ID
   - Intel IMOD minimum timing workaround
   - AMD PLL quirk
   - ASMedia delay requirements
   - VIA VL805 reset-on-resume (Raspberry Pi 4)
   - Fresco Logic, Renesas, Etron handling

2. USB 3.1/3.2 Protocol Speed ID (PSIV) support:
   - Parse extended protocol capability for USB 3.1+ speeds
   - Detect SuperSpeed+ ports with proper speed information
   - Support for Gen1x1/Gen2x1/Gen1x2/Gen2x2 speeds

3. Enhanced error recovery:
   - Error-specific recovery strategies
   - Consecutive error tracking to detect broken devices
   - Better handling of transaction, stall, and babble errors

4. Additional hardware definitions:
   - PCI vendor/device IDs for common xHCI controllers
   - HCCPARAMS2 for xHCI 1.1+ capabilities
   - PSI (Protocol Speed ID) parsing macros

5. Fixes carried forward from previous patches:
   - Zero-bandwidth endpoint support for UVC cameras
   - MSI-X disabled due to TRB errors on some controllers
   - Proper endpoint initialization with max_burst fields
   - Safety check in SubmitNormalRequest for unconfigured endpoints

Signed-off-by: Haiku UVC Webcam Project
